// Built-in present shader of the RSX backend (vertex stage).
//
// Draws the intermediate screen surface as a full-screen quad into the display buffer. This is where the
// engine's OpenGL bottom-up convention becomes the scan-out's top-down one - but the flip lives in the
// quad's vertex data (see RsxDevice::CreateBuiltinResources), not here, so this stage stays a plain
// pass-through and the one convention correction is in a single readable place.
//
// Not generated from a .shader file: it has no GLSL counterpart because no other backend needs it.
void main
(
	float2 aPosition : POSITION,
	float2 aTexCoords : TEXCOORD0,

	out float4 ePosition : POSITION,
	out float2 vTexCoords : TEXCOORD0
)
{
	ePosition = float4(aPosition.x, aPosition.y, 0.0f, 1.0f);
	vTexCoords = aTexCoords;
}
